# The sandbox environment — a template.
#
# The real file lives on the VPS at $HOME/proxiapay-sandbox/.env.sandbox, is
# chmod 600, and is never committed. Copy this there and fill in every <…>.
#
# It is named `sandbox.env.example` rather than `.env.sandbox.example` only
# because a dot-env name is unwritable under this machine's tooling guard; the
# file it becomes on the VPS carries the ordinary name.

# ── What Compose itself reads ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# WITHOUT THIS LINE NOTHING STARTS, and the error does not say so plainly.
# `--env-file` on the command line governs only the ${…} interpolation in the
# compose file; the services declare `env_file: ${ENV_FILE:-.env.production}`.
# Unset, they ask for a .env.production that does not exist here, and the deploy
# dies on "env file … not found" after pulling every image.
ENV_FILE=.env.sandbox

# Separates the Compose project, the container names and the Traefik routers
# from any other stack built from this repository. See the header of
# docker-compose.deploy.yml for what a shared name costs.
STACK=proxiapay-sandbox

# One hostname serves everything. The console's only call to the platform is
# relative, so the bundle and the API must share an origin. Traefik sends /v1,
# /console, /providers and /docs to the api, and everything else to the console.
APP_DOMAIN=sandbox.pay.proxia-digital.com

# `le` validates by TLS-ALPN-01, which requires the name to reach this VPS
# directly. It does today: sandbox.pay.proxia-digital.com is a plain A record,
# unlike the apex, which sits behind Cloudflare. THE DAY THIS NAME GOES BEHIND
# THE ORANGE CLOUD, switch to `le-dns`: Cloudflare terminates TLS itself, the
# ALPN challenge never reaches Traefik, and the failure is silent until the
# renewal sixty days later.
CERT_RESOLVER=le

REGISTRY=ghcr.io/iamvaln
IMAGE_TAG=develop

# ── What the platform reads ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `sandbox` selects the simulator provider account at seed time and lets a
# project exist without declared origins (spec 2.3). No provider credentials are
# needed here: the seed points the account at simulator://local.
PROXIAPAY_ENV=sandbox
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=3000
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Its own database, with its own password — never a copy of production's.
POSTGRES_USER=proxiapay_sandbox
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<generate: openssl rand -hex 24>
POSTGRES_DB=proxiapay_sandbox
DATABASE_URL=postgres://proxiapay_sandbox:<the same password>@db:5432/proxiapay_sandbox

# THESE TWO ARE A DOCUMENTED DEVIATION. docs/operations.md says neither belongs
# in a file on the host — they should be injected from a key store at process
# start. This VPS has no key store, so for the SANDBOX they live here, mode 600,
# holding nothing but simulator traffic. Production must not copy this choice.
# Generate each with: openssl rand -base64 32
MASTER_KEY_BASE64=<generate>
INDEX_KEY_BASE64=<generate>

# Same origin as the console, used for the cookie attributes and CORS.
CONSOLE_ORIGIN=https://sandbox.pay.proxia-digital.com

# Mail goes through Resend. MAIL_FROM must sit on a domain verified there;
# proxia-digital.com is, and routes from eu-west-1.
RESEND_API_KEY=<the Resend key>
MAIL_FROM=ProxiaPay Sandbox <sandbox@proxia-digital.com>

# Where alerts land. The three group addresses are seeded once into each group's
# delivery addresses; the console owns them afterwards. A group without one
# falls back to ALERT_EMAIL.
ALERT_EMAIL=<your address>
ALERT_EMAIL_FINANCE=
ALERT_EMAIL_DEVELOPERS=
ALERT_EMAIL_ADMINISTRATORS=
